  "finding_info": {
    "uid": "d00ec57ca1e00a1a8e6df7424795d062",
    "title": "Agent modified its own harness configuration",
    "desc": "An agent account wrote its own harness config - the settings that grant its permissions, the hooks that run on every tool call, the MCP servers it loads, or its instruction files. A human edits ~/.claude/settings.json by hand; the *agent* widening its own allow-list, adding a hook, registering an MCP server or editing CLAUDE.md is the purest form of prompt-injection persistence: the next session re-reads the file and the injection is now policy. Auto-memory writes (projects/*/memory/*) are excluded - the agent writes those constantly by design, and memory *poisoning* is a content problem banken cannot see. This detection has no SigmaHQ equivalent; it is specific to an agent that can rewrite its own leash.",
